/**
 * Tests for order splitting logic.
 *
 * An OrderSplitter takes an Order (line items + fulfillment preferences) and
 * warehouse inventory, and produces the minimum set of Shipments required to
 * fulfil the order given the following hard constraints:
 *
 *   1. Items with different fulfillment types (SHIP_TO_HOME vs STORE_PICKUP)
 *      must be in separate shipments.
 *   2. Items destined for different delivery addresses must be in separate
 *      shipments.
 *   3. In-stock items must not be held back to wait for pre-order/backordered
 *      items — each item ships when available.
 *   4. A single shipment can only be sourced from one warehouse.
 *   5. The total number of shipments must be minimised.
 *
 * And one soft constraint (honoured when possible without increasing shipment
 * count):
 *
 *   - Companion items (e.g. camera body + matching lens marked as a companion
 *     group) should ship together from the same warehouse.
 */
